<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bashir Shihab II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1850">1850</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bashir Shihab II was emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a> from 1789 to 1840, the most powerful ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shihab-dynasty">Shihab dynasty</a>. Born a Muslim, he became a Maronite Christian and broke the power of rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> lords. He built the palace of Beiteddine and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</a> in the 1830s. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> out in 1840, he was exiled.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bashir-shihab-ii.jpg" alt="Bashir Shihab II" width="287" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daoud Corm d. 1930 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BashirChehab.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
